| info = *Rhino expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] to harden his skin, receiving {{D|Overguard}} equal to {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''400 / 600 / 800 / 1200''' plus {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''100% / 125% / 175% / 250%''' of his total armor. Upon activation, Rhino is invulnerable for <u>'''1.5 / 2 / 3 / 3'''</u> seconds, during which all incoming damage is absorbed and added to the Overguard.
**Iron Skin's Overguard uses the following equation:<br/>{{MathText|Overguard {{eql}} ([Base Overguard + (Armor Multiplier {{mul}} Total Armor)] {{mul}} Ability Strength) + Absorbed Damage}} where {{MathText|Total Armor {{eql}} (Base Armor {{mul}} [1 + Armor Mods]) + Additive Armor}}.
***Note that the base armor value is different between {{WF|Rhino}} and {{WF|Rhino Prime}}; while Rhino has '''240''' Base Armor, Rhino Prime has '''290''' Base Armor.
****As an example for '''Rhino''':
*****With a maxed {{M|Steel Fiber}} and {{M|Intensify}}, a Rank 3 Iron Skin cast by Rhino will have an initial Overguard of {{Math|(1200 + (2.5 {{mul}} 240 {{mul}} 2)) {{mul}} 1.3|mt=y}} before absorbing damage.
****Modifying that equation for '''Rhino Prime''':
*****With a maxed {{M|Steel Fiber}} and {{M|Intensify}}, a Rank 3 Iron Skin cast by Rhino Prime will have an initial Overguard of {{Math|(1200 + (2.5 {{mul}} 290 {{mul}} 2)) {{mul}} 1.3|mt=y}} before absorbing damage.
**The {{D|Overguard}} is purely ability-based, it is '''not''' "real" like overguard gained by {{A|Recompense}} or {{Arcane|Secondary Fortifier}}, it can be removed by ability nullifying effects.
| synergies =
